conch.app carries tmux 3.7c (https://github.com/tmux/tmux) at
Contents/Helpers/tmux. conch runs it as a separate program to host its own
sessions; nothing of tmux is linked into conch.

tmux is distributed under the ISC licence: see COPYING beside this notice,
unmodified from the tmux source tree. The code tmux compiles in from its
compat/ directory on macOS carries its own ISC and BSD notices, collected
verbatim in LICENSE.compat.

That one binary has three libraries linked into it statically, each under its
own licence, included beside this notice unmodified from its source tree:

  libevent 2.1.13-stable  BSD 3-clause (and the notices of its parts)  LICENSE.libevent
  jemalloc 5.3.1          BSD 2-clause                                  COPYING.jemalloc
  utf8proc 2.11.3         MIT, and the Unicode data licence             LICENSE.utf8proc.md

The terminal database is read through macOS's own ncurses
(/usr/lib/libncurses.5.4.dylib), which conch does not ship.

None of these licences asks for the source to travel with the binary. It was
built with no changes to any source: the pinned versions, the sha256 of every
source tarball and the exact configure and make invocations are in
scripts/fetch-tmux.sh in conch's source.
